OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`. That path is
NOT a project.yml source group in this repo. The real, compiled canonical admin-page home is
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` — where the sibling P7 admin pages (ApiPlaygroundPage,
DiskForecastPage) ship, and which project.yml already lists as a `Sources` source path for BOTH the
iOS (`TeslaSync`) and macOS (`TeslaSync-macOS`) app targets (createIntermediateGroups: true). The
page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, the faithful equivalent of the
prompt's `Features/Admin`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the identical
reconciliation the ApiPlayground + DiskForecast logs recorded; it is the only deviation from the
literal prompt path. xcodegen confirms inclusion: "FleetAPI" referenced 42x in the generated
pbxproj (iOS + macOS app targets + both XCTest bundles).

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route `/fleet-api` is a standalone top-level route (web App.tsx), unlike
DiskForecast's `/admin/disk-forecast` sub-path (which folds onto `.admin`). It had no AppRoute case,
so a `.fleetAPI` case was added (pathSegment "fleet-api", systemImage "network", System group) —
"navigation registration" is an allowed file class. `AppRouteParser.parse("/fleet-api")` and the
deep link `teslasync://fleet-api` now resolve to it (segment match). `FleetAPIRouteRegistration`
registers `.fleetAPI -> FleetAPIPage` and is chained into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift,
mirroring ApiPlayground/DiskForecast registration (model built on MainActor + captured, so the
escaping registry closure never constructs an isolated type). The pre-existing RouteTests
(testEveryRouteHasUniquePathSegment / testEveryRouteResolvesToItsGroup) remain satisfied — the new
case has a unique segment and resolves to the System group.

