================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI FleetAPIPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure @Observable
state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/loaded/error over an injectable
FleetAPIDataSource seam whose 6 methods keep the web hook names and whose value types mirror the web
AppSettings/PollingConfig/CaptureStats/VersionInfo 1:1 (production binds the KMP settings store through
the seam). The page reproduces the web chrome (title/subtitle), the Tesla API Polling card (suspend
Toggle + suspended notice), the API Endpoint Controls card (polling/on-demand/command adaptive toggle
grids + the MongoDB-gated Telemetry Capture group with retention Select and captured-signal summary),
and the Configured Endpoints card (version line + endpoint URL rows or EmptyState) — eight GlassPanel
peers in all, using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass), adaptive across
macOS/iPad/iPhone. The page's mutations raise the web success/info/error toasts via a transient
TSAlertBanner overlay. Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names
(71 keys added). Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an
executed model harness (39/39); the full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to pre-existing, out-of-scope
shared-surfaces/feature-views breakage (baseline-rebuild-proven), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

